1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,700
Every clan event starts the same way.

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:06,900
Someone says, "we should do a bingo."

3
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:08,920
Everyone agrees.

4
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:12,501
And then one person spends the next two weeks in a spreadsheet,

5
00:00:12,501 --> 00:00:15,740
squinting at screenshots of other people's Vorkath kills.

6
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:19,170
Today, that person retires.

7
00:00:24,970 --> 00:00:29,080
Open your clan's Manage page, then Events.

8
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:31,510
This is mission control.

9
00:00:31,510 --> 00:00:34,613
Live events, drafts, things that already ended,

10
00:00:34,613 --> 00:00:37,240
and a button that says Create event.

11
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:39,590
We're going to press it.

12
00:00:39,590 --> 00:00:40,600
Bravely.

13
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:43,830
Step one: a name.

14
00:00:43,830 --> 00:00:47,290
Something inspiring, like "Autumn Ladder."

15
00:00:47,290 --> 00:00:50,660
Nobody has ever been this creative.

16
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:52,320
Then a format.

17
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:55,600
Standard is a plain list of tasks.

18
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:59,940
Bingo is a grid, with bonus points for finishing lines.

19
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:05,270
The fancier formats get their own episodes, because they need the emotional support.

20
00:01:06,070 --> 00:01:08,570
Step two: when it runs.

21
00:01:08,570 --> 00:01:11,170
A start, an end, done.

22
00:01:11,170 --> 00:01:14,282
Or make it repeat, say every weekend this month,

23
00:01:14,282 --> 00:01:17,830
and between windows it simply ignores everyone.

24
00:01:17,830 --> 00:01:20,780
All times are UTC.

25
00:01:20,780 --> 00:01:22,720
Game time.

26
00:01:22,720 --> 00:01:25,770
No daylight savings surprises.

27
00:01:26,570 --> 00:01:29,880
Step three: how people get on teams.

28
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:35,290
They pick their own, get auto-balanced, drop into a sign-up pool you sort out later,

29
00:01:35,290 --> 00:01:39,340
or you assign everyone by hand, like a benevolent dictator.

30
00:01:39,340 --> 00:01:42,710
Down here you choose which submissions count.

31
00:01:42,710 --> 00:01:48,770
Everything, plugin only, or anything typed in manually needs an admin's thumbs up.

32
00:01:48,770 --> 00:01:51,020
Trust is a spectrum.

33
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:54,270
Step four: tasks.

34
00:01:54,270 --> 00:01:57,600
Build them one at a time, grab presets from the library,

35
00:01:57,600 --> 00:02:01,584
or hit Fill for me, and DropTracker drafts a balanced list based on

36
00:02:01,584 --> 00:02:05,520
how long the event runs and how much your clan actually plays.

37
00:02:05,520 --> 00:02:09,900
The options are casual, regular, and very active.

38
00:02:09,900 --> 00:02:11,260
Be honest.

39
00:02:11,260 --> 00:02:14,460
Episode two covers tasks properly.

40
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:17,630
Step five: teams.

41
00:02:17,630 --> 00:02:18,924
Type a name, add it,

42
00:02:18,924 --> 00:02:22,860
paste in a list of players if you already know who's who.

43
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:26,480
Or skip it and let people sign themselves up.

44
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:29,860
Your clan, your call, your group chat drama.

45
00:02:30,660 --> 00:02:33,160
Step six: Discord.

46
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:38,790
Pick where announcements go, where completions go, and where the live leaderboard lives.

47
00:02:38,790 --> 00:02:42,810
It can even create a private channel and a role for every team,

48
00:02:42,810 --> 00:02:45,160
then tidy them up afterwards.

49
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:47,100
Like a butler.

50
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:49,120
A butler who pings.

51
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:52,760
Last step: the pre-flight check.

52
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:55,780
If it's all green, launch it now.

53
00:02:55,780 --> 00:02:59,130
Or keep it as a draft and walk away.

54
00:02:59,130 --> 00:03:03,870
Drafts don't expire, don't cost anything, and never ask how you're doing.

55
00:03:04,670 --> 00:03:07,340
Here's what your players see.

56
00:03:07,340 --> 00:03:11,830
The board, the standings, their team, and a big sign up button.

57
00:03:11,830 --> 00:03:15,050
And from then on, they just play the game.

58
00:03:15,050 --> 00:03:20,094
The RuneLite plugin sends their drops, kills and personal bests to DropTracker,

59
00:03:20,094 --> 00:03:22,010
and the board fills itself in.

60
00:03:22,810 --> 00:03:25,860
Nobody posts screenshots.

61
00:03:25,860 --> 00:03:28,180
Nobody checks them.

62
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:30,780
The spreadsheet person is free.

63
00:03:32,580 --> 00:03:35,130
Next time: tasks.

64
00:03:35,130 --> 00:03:39,550
What counts, what doesn't, and why Turael skipping will not save you.
